e ambiguity, the key point is that the reason compares the sum of outcome differences, and it prefers the lottery with the more favorable (likely positive) sum. In this case, the sum of differences (in a pairwise sense) is 6000 (from 0 vs -6000) and 3000 (from 0 vs -3000), but the net sum across all pairs is 6000. The reason is applicable because the outcomes and probabilities are given and the pairwise differences can be computed.",
