  "step_3": "The decision reason requires the individual to compute the sum of pairwise differences of outcomes between the lotteries and prefer the one with the more favorable (less negative) sum. In this case, the sum of pairwise differences favors A (positive 4990) over B (negative -4990). However, the individual does not compute or refer to any such sum. Instead, the individual focuses on the probability of the large loss in B and perceives it as very unlikely, thus choosing B. The justification is based on risk probability, not on the sum of outcome differences. Therefore, the individual did not use the decision reason. The information considered (probability of large loss) is not equivalent to the sum of pairwise differences of outcomes. The justification does not follow the rule of the decision reason. Thus, the decision reason was not used.",
